.Dd November 2, 2026
.Dt RFKILL 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm rfkill
.Nd list, block and unblock radio switches
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Cm list
.Op Ar index Ns | Ns Ar type
.Nm
.Cm block
.Ar index Ns | Ns Ar type
.Nm
.Cm unblock
.Ar index Ns | Ns Ar type
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is BusyBox's applet for the kernel's radio switches.
Each radio has a switch, numbered from 0, with a type, a soft block that
software sets and clears, and a hard block that a key or a switch of the
machine sets.
A radio transmits only while neither is set.
.Pp
.Cm list
prints each switch, or those of the
.Ar index
or
.Ar type
given, as its index, name and type, and whether it is soft and hard
blocked.
.Cm block
sets the soft block of the switches named, and
.Cm unblock
clears it; a hard block stays until the machine clears it.
.Pp
A
.Ar type
is
.Cm all ,
.Cm wlan
or
.Cm wifi ,
.Cm bluetooth ,
.Cm uwb
or
.Cm ultrawideband ,
.Cm wimax ,
.Cm wwan ,
.Cm gps
or
.Cm fm .
Anything else is taken as an
.Ar index .
.Pp
.Cm block
and
.Cm unblock
need write access to
.Pa /dev/rfkill ,
which root has.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /dev/rfkill
The device the switches are read and changed through.
.It Pa /sys/class/rfkill/rfkill Ns Ar N Ns Pa /uevent
The name and type of switch
.Ar N ,
which
.Cm list
prints.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
Stop and restart every Wi-Fi radio:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
rfkill block wifi
rfkill unblock wifi
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr rfkill 4 ,
.Xr iw 8 ,
.Xr wpa_supplicant 8
